WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:16.700
When Peter went down into Dorfli that evening, he saw a knot of people a little way off

2
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.260
the path.

3
00:00:18.461 --> 00:00:20.963
He wriggled through the crowd to see what they were looking at.

4
00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:25.086
"I saw it when they came through town," said the pastor.

5
00:00:25.106 --> 00:00:27.949
"It must have cost a lot of money."

6
00:00:27.969 --> 00:00:32.921
"I wonder how it was broken," a woman said.

7
00:00:32.941 --> 00:00:38.566
"I don't know," remarked the baker, "but someone will suffer for it.

8
00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:42.689
The gentleman in Frankfurt will want the matter investigated."

9
00:00:44.571 --> 00:00:45.972
It was the ruined wheelchair!

10
00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:53.798
The baker's words frightened Peter and he hurried home, afraid that a policeman might arrive from Frankfurt any

11
00:00:53.858 --> 00:01:00.264
moment. The days that followed were the most joyous days Heidi and Clara spent on the mountain.

12
00:01:03.352 --> 00:01:09.015
Clara awoke each morning with a happy voice inside her that said, "I am well!

13
00:01:09.616 --> 00:01:12.277
I can walk by myself, like other people!"

14
00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:18.260
Every day, she practiced walking with Grandfather, and every day, it got easier.

15
00:01:19.761 --> 00:01:27.025
The exercise gave her quite an appetite, so Grandfather started cutting her bread and cheese in thicker slices.

16
00:01:28.306 --> 00:01:33.689
He also brought out a large jug of foaming milk at every meal and filled her bowl over

17
00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:34.450
and over.

18
00:01:36.271 --> 00:01:39.734
During the week, Heidi noticed that Peter was acting strangely.

19
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:46.460
He never asked if she was coming up the mountain in the morning, but ran off with the

20
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.664
goats as soon as Grandfather let Daisy and Dusky out of their pen.

21
00:01:52.485 --> 00:02:00.432
When Heidi asked Grandfather about Peter's behavior, he replied, "Perhaps Peter fears punishment for something he has done."

22
00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:05.114
Heidi and Clara had planned to give Grandmamma a big surprise.

23
00:02:06.455 --> 00:02:12.338
When she arrived on her horse the next afternoon, she saw Heidi and Clara sitting on the grass

24
00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:13.719
under the fir trees.

25
00:02:14.919 --> 00:02:16.800
She quickly climbed down from her horse.

26
00:02:18.001 --> 00:02:20.602
"Why aren't you resting in your chair, Clara?"

27
00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:22.083
she asked, worried.

28
00:02:23.544 --> 00:02:27.326
As she got closer, she said, "Is it really you?

29
00:02:28.046 --> 00:02:30.648
Your cheeks are so round and rosy!

30
00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:33.797
I hardly recognize you!"

31
00:02:34.897 --> 00:02:40.139
It was then that Clara and Heidi stood up and walked over to her, as if it were

32
00:02:40.179 --> 00:02:41.820
the most normal thing in the world.

33
00:02:45.401 --> 00:02:47.662
Grandmamma could hardly believe her eyes.

34
00:02:48.863 --> 00:02:52.824
Laughing and crying, she embraced them both over and over again.

35
00:02:53.985 --> 00:02:56.966
She caught sight of Grandfather looking on and smiling.

36
00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.188
"My dear Grandfather!

37
00:03:02.584 --> 00:03:05.146
I do believe this is all your doing!"

38
00:03:05.527 --> 00:03:06.387
said Grandmamma.

39
00:03:06.407 --> 00:03:09.890
"How much we have to thank you for!"

40
00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.494
"You can thank God's good sunshine and mountain air!"

41
00:03:14.955 --> 00:03:16.256
said Grandfather, smiling.

42
00:03:16.276 --> 00:03:21.360
"Yes, and don't forget the beautiful milk," said Clara.

43
00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.765
"You wouldn't believe how much I have been drinking and how good it is!"

44
00:03:26.785 --> 00:03:30.528
"I can see by your cheeks, Clara.

45
00:03:31.552 --> 00:03:34.134
But we must really telegraph your father.

46
00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.096
He must come see you at once!"

47
00:03:37.656 --> 00:03:38.857
exclaimed Grandmamma.

48
00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:45.582
So when Peter arrived with the goats a short time later, Grandmamma gave him a note to take

49
00:03:45.622 --> 00:03:47.483
to the telegraph office in Dorfli.

50
00:03:49.124 --> 00:03:54.067
Meanwhile, Clara's father, Herr Sesemann, had prepared a little surprise of his own.

51
00:03:55.328 --> 00:04:02.256
He had changed his schedule and, at that very moment, was walking up the mountainside.

52
00:04:02.276 --> 00:04:07.698
He paused, hot and tired from the walk, and saw Peter running down the path with the note

53
00:04:07.718 --> 00:04:08.238
in his hand.

54
00:04:08.258 --> 00:04:09.938
"You lad!

55
00:04:10.398 --> 00:04:15.060
Come here," he cried, meaning to ask if he was on the right path to Grandfather's hut.

56
00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.660
"The policeman!"

57
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:18.681
thought Peter.

58
00:04:19.861 --> 00:04:24.862
He let out a frightened cry, ran off the path, and found a large tree to hide behind.

59
00:04:24.882 --> 00:04:28.563
"Oh my," said Herr Sesemann to himself.

60
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:30.904
"What a shy boy!"

61
00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:34.883
And turning to face the mountain path, he resumed his climb.
